# Ops loop

You are working in a git-tracked Obsidian vault at `docs/` — the company OS lives in `docs/ops/`.

- Start from `docs/ops/HOME.md` and `docs/ops/BOARD.md` (regenerate with `python3 ops/scripts/board_sync.py`).
- **`main` docs = company state.** Primary clone stays on `main`. Docs-only: short-lived **worktree** from `origin/main`, docs PR, delete branch + remove worktree after merge, confirm `main` CI green (else fix). If already in a `wf/…` / `prd/…` worktree for code, fold docs into that PR. Layout: `docs/ops/workflow/WORKTREES.md`.
- Prefer no human in the loop; `gate: human` / `blocked` are the exception.
- Roles: planner lands plans on `main`. Implementer uses a sibling worktree after `implement` on `main`. Reviewer comments; may Approve or Request changes — never merge from chat. Ready PRs squash-merge when CI is green **and** a valid non-author `APPROVED` exists. Mock-prod VPS tracks `main` only.
- One ticket per session. Skip `type: epic`. Prefix `WF-` = workflow. `PRD-` = product. `INC-` = incident.
- New tickets: `python3 ops/scripts/new_ticket.py`. Naming: `docs/ops/NAMING.md`. Roster: `docs/ops/agents/_index.md`.
- App code is disposable scaffolding (`docs/ops/company/SCAFFOLDING.md`). Do not polish it.
- CI is Jenkins (house) + GitHub Actions dual-run. No GitHub production Environment (probably never). Decision 39: this product’s host is https://fishing-journals.com (one VPS until a later split). No secrets in notes. Current build: `docs/product/FREE-DIRECTORY.md` (pipeline, then the free directory). Do not promote the booking checkout program.
- Full loop: `docs/ops/workflow/LOOP.md`. Worktrees: `docs/ops/workflow/WORKTREES.md`. CI: `docs/ops/workflow/CI.md`. Safety: `docs/ops/workflow/SAFETY.md`.
- Do not implement product unless `PRD-*` and `status: implement`.
